# Word of Command (CR 723.2, 608.2g, 733.1): Bone Splinters forced on Bot2, whose only {B} is Phyrexian Tower's "{T},
# Sacrifice a creature: Add {B}{B}" and whose only creature, Memnite, is also what Bone Splinters must sacrifice. The
# cast can never be completed. Bot1 tries the Tower, sacrificing Memnite to it; the attempt is reversed, Memnite back. Made
# again, the Tower is tried again, and its sacrifice has only the dead Memnite to offer: the engine ends the attempt there itself,
# and then every answer above it is dead - the Tower, then the target -
# so nothing is cast, nothing is asked that will be refused, and the game goes on - both cards where
# they were, Memnite alive, the Ornithopter unharmed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Word of Command
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Tower
Memnite
Bone Splinters
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Tower.Play
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Bone Splinters)
Bot2.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)
Bot2.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Activate(Ability: Sacrifice)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Hand.Bone Splinters.Colors = Black
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite; Phyrexian Tower
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Tower.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
